# What the host shell sources or runs from this tree on its own, which
# claude-sandbox (github:Runeword/claude-sandbox) pins read-only on top of its
# read-write bind of the tree: writable, each one would let a session run code
# on the host before a diff could be reviewed. One path per line, relative to
# sources/, `#` starting a comment. Read at every launch and pinned itself,
# like everything it names, so it is edited from a plain terminal.
#
# Claude's own config: settings*.json (hooks, permissions), hooks/, the plugin
# .mcp.json manifests, rules/, and git-allowlist.toml, which the git-shim
# re-reads on every call — writable, it would let a session widen its own
# allowlist mid-run.
.claude
# The shell startup chain: .zshrc plus its glob-sourced plugins, .bashrc, the
# three files both rc files source by name, and functions/, sourced by glob —
# a new file there would be executed too, so the directory is pinned, not its
# files. functions/claude.bash is what starts the sandbox.
.config/zsh
.config/bash
.config/shell/xdg.sh
.config/shell/variables.sh
.config/shell/aliases.sh
.config/shell/functions
# The leader-key command table: aliases.sh's __aliases widget (pinned above)
# renders it and runs the picked chord's cmd in the host shell — accept-line
# for the default run mode, eval for eval entries — on every leader press.
# Writable, a session could rewrite a familiar chord into its own host command;
# this is the data the pinned widget executes, moved out of the pinned
# functions/ dir, so pinned with it.
.config/shell/leader.toml
# GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL for the wrapped git — so for the git-shim, and for
# starship at every prompt: core.hooksPath would sidestep the launcher's
# .git/hooks lock, and core.fsmonitor, `!` aliases and filters run commands
# outright.
.config/git
# delta, git's core.pager, runs the command its config's `pager` key names, at
# every paged git diff, log or show on the host: the `git diff -- sources` that
# reviews a session included.
.config/delta
# direnvrc runs in the host shell at every cd; the launcher's .direnv and CAS
# locks guard direnv's outputs, this guards its input.
.config/direnv
#
# Left writable on purpose: on-demand tool config (bat, navi, ripgrep, readline,
# nvim-fzf, tree-sitter), the fzf scripts under shell/scripts/, and — the repo's
# main editing target, though the host runs them unprompted too — the tmux,
# starship and alacritty configs. Add them here if that trade-off changes.
# Review of the writable rest is `git diff -- sources` on the host.
